    {
      "id": "ded68fcb1fc2f254bd0bef4906fc309796a2b870",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2472185034,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> Should `ABSOLUTE_TIME_NTP_UTC` as a display type (where 0 means \"unknown/null\") be deprecated and replaced with this?\n\nYes. Different uses of `ABSOLUTE_TIME_NTP_UTC` may have different strings for the special case.\n\nUnfortunately, I'm not sure you can mark a `#define` as deprecated, so that you'll get compile-time warnings; at best, we could add a run-time warning when a field using it is registered.\n\nI figure I'll first commit this, and then various cases that it handles can be changed to use it.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-04-27T20:01:02.196Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-04-27T20:01:02.196Z",
